{
  "title": "Distal Clavicle Osteolysis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3048/distal-clavicle-osteolysis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 3 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Distal clavicle osteolysis is the painful development of bony erosions and resorption of the distal clavicle caused by repetitive trauma to the AC joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs of the shoulder revealing osteolysis, cysts, erosions and resorption of the distal end of the clavicle.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a trial of NSAIDs, activity modifications, and corticosteroid injections. Arthroscopic versus open distal clavicle excision is indicated for patients with persistent symptoms that have failed nonoperative treatment.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patients in their 20s, mostly male",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "commonly seen in weightlifters",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "history of traumatic injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "caused by **repetitive stress and micro-fracture** in distal clavicle which leads to osteopenia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "clavicle is",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "S-shaped bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "last bone to fuse",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Medial growth plate fuses early 20s",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diarthrodial joint with fibrocartilage meniscus",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Ligamentous",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "AC ligaments: horizontal stability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "CC ligaments: vertical stability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Similar to AC joint arthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "located at distal clavicle and anterior superior shoulder",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "insidious in onset",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "exacerbated by repetitive loading (ie. bench press or push-ups)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tenderness at the distal end of clavicle and AC joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain with cross-body adduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP clavicle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Zanca view (15 degrees cephalad tilt)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3048/images/zanca_view_method..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings of the distal clavicle (should not involve the acromion)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3048/images/distal%20clavicle%20osteolysis.jpg",
                  "caption": "shows distal osteolysis"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cysts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3048/images/distal_clav..jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows osteolysis"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "osteopenia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "resorption and erosion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tapering of distal clavicle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "AC joint widening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Advanced Imaging",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "MRI: increased signal of T2 sequences and bone marrow edema",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "bone scan: increased uptake in the distal clavicle (may be seen earlier than radiographic changes)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity modification, NSAIDs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "modification",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "avoid aggravating weight-lifting exercises or modify technique",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "ie. moving hand grip closer together and ending weight descent to 4 to 6 cm above the chest",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "corticosteroid injections",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "diagnostic and therapeutic",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "more accurate with ultrasound",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open or arthroscopic distal clavicle excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "persistent symptoms that have failed nonoperative treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**technique**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**need to address associated pathology to the rotator cuff and long head of biceps**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**open vs. arthroscopic based on surgeon preference and comfort**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "arthroscopic resection has the advantage of allowing evaluation of the glenohumeral joint",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "good results are shown with arthroscopic treatment",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "5",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "**quicker recovery and return to activity**",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "4",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "open procedures require meticulous repair of deltoid-trapezial fascia",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Arthroscopic distal clavicle resection (Mumford procedure)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "should **resect only 0.5-1cm** of the distal clavicle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**too large a resection can lead to AC joint instability**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Horizontal instability**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "avoid violating the posterosuperior capsule during distal clavicle excision as will lead to horizontal instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
